# Excluding Document Formats

To leave some source documents out of the generated site, use the [`moduleExcludes`](../site-mojo.html${esc.hash}moduleExcludes) parameter. Each entry is named after a source format, such as `markdown`, `apt`, `xdoc` or `fml`, and holds a comma-separated list of file names or patterns, relative to the directory of that format.

For example, your project has the following site content:

```
Module1
|-- src
|   `-- site
|       |-- markdown
|       |   `-- index.md
|       `-- fml
|           `-- sample-fml.fml
`-- pom.xml
```

To exclude all the documents in the FML format from the generated site, set the following in your POM and run `mvn site`:

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <build>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-site-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <moduleExcludes>
            <fml>*.fml</fml>
          </moduleExcludes>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
  ...
</project>
```

The generated site then contains no `sample-fml.html`, and the build log counts only the remaining documents:

```
[INFO] Rendering 1 Doxia document: 1 markdown
```

See the documentation of the [moduleExcludes](../site-mojo.html#moduleExcludes) Mojo parameter for more details.

